SUMMARY:Full Moon · Nobbys Lighthouse from Stockton foreshore · Moonrise 
 behind Nobbys Head
LOCATION:Stockton Ferry Wharf and foreshore\, Mitchell Street\, Stockton NS
 W 2295
GEO:-32.92094;151.78193
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=-32.92094,151.78193
DESCRIPTION:WHAT: The full moon rising out of the Tasman Sea behind Nobbys 
 Head Lighthouse\, across the mouth of Newcastle Harbour. Big ships often p
 ass in front.\nTarget: moon centred on the lighthouse lantern on Nobbys He
 ad.\n\nWHEN (Sydney time)\nSunday 21 February 2027\nFull moon: Sun 21 Feb 
 10:23. Moon 100% lit at the alignment.\nSunset 19:38 · civil twilight end
 s 20:03\nMoonrise 19:45 at azimuth 81° E (sea level horizon).\nALIGNMENT 
 19:52: moon altitude 1.2°\, azimuth 80.3°.\nArrive by 19:07. The moon mo
 ves about one diameter every 2 to 3 minutes\, so shoot from 10 minutes bef
 ore to 10 minutes after.\n\nMOON TRACK\n19:45  altitude -0.0°\, azimuth  
 81.2°\n19:50  altitude  0.9°\, azimuth  80.5°  << alignment\n19:55  alt
 itude  1.8°\, azimuth  79.9°\n20:00  altitude  2.7°\, azimuth  79.2°\n
 20:05  altitude  3.7°\, azimuth  78.6°\n\nCAMERA POSITION\nExact alignme
 nt pin: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=-32.92094\,151.781
 93\nNamed spot: Stockton Ferry Wharf and foreshore\, Mitchell Street\, Sto
 ckton NSW 2295 (144 m from the exact pin). https://www.google.com/maps/sea
 rch/?api=1&query=-32.91974\,151.78250\nSubject pin (Nobbys Lighthouse): ht
 tps://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=-32.91857\,151.79840\nFrom t
 he exact pin\, Nobbys Lighthouse is 1560 m away on bearing 80.3°.\nFrom t
 he named spot it is on bearing 85.0°\, so there the moon passes 4.7° lef
 t of the target. Walk toward the exact pin to close the gap.\nStraight lin
 e from Neutral Bay: about 114 km.\n\nTIDES (BOM prediction\, Newcastle)\nT
 he Newcastle gauge is in the same harbour mouth\, so times are close.\nLow
  water Sun 15:57  0.21 m\nHigh water Sun 22:05  1.66 m\nAt the alignment (
 19:52): about 1.24 m and rising.\nPredictions exclude swell\, wind setup a
 nd wave run up. Check BOM coastal waters and swell forecasts on the day.\n
 Source table: https://www.bom.gov.au/ntc/IDO59001/IDO59001_2027_NSW_TP004.
 pdf\n\nFRAMING (Sony A1)\nNobbys Lighthouse spans about 0.7° tall from he
 re. The moon is 0.52° wide\, about 14 m across at this distance.\nLandmar
 k filling 60% of the frame height: FE 70-200mm F2.8 GM OSS II with the 2x 
 teleconverter at 400 mm\, or about 600 mm equivalent in APS-C crop mode.\n
 Moon dominant: FE 70-200mm F2.8 GM OSS II with the 2x teleconverter at 400
  mm (f/5.6) puts the moon at 15% of frame height (23% in APS-C crop mode).
 \nTripod\, OSS off on the tripod\, 2 s timer or remote\, shutter 1/125 s o
 r faster at 400 mm.\nStart: ISO 200 to 400\, f/8\, expose for the moon. Br
 acket 3 frames at 2 EV after sunset and blend.\n\nFIELD NOTES\n- Stockton 
 is reached by the Newcastle ferry from Queens Wharf or by road over Stockt
 on Bridge.\n- Harbour traffic: check the Port of Newcastle shipping schedu
 le for a ship in frame.\n- The camera pin is on the foreshore south of the
  wharf. Walk the shoreline to fine tune.\n- Stay off the breakwall when th
 ere is any surf.\n\nVERIFY BEFORE YOU GO\nTPE Web (camera pin\, subject pi
 n\, alignment time): https://app.photoephemeris.com/?ll=-32.92094\,151.781
 93&center=-32.92094\,151.78193&z=16&dt=2027-02-21T08%3A52%3A00.000Z&sll=-3
 2.91857\,151.79840&fovb=80.3&fovhfov=5.14&fovvfov=3.44&fovd=1560&fovo=l&fo
 vov=1\nIn TPE\, set the secondary height to about 18 m above ground to che
 ck the geodetics line.\nPhotoPills: Planner > red pin on the camera pin\, 
 black pin on the subject > Find > Moon\, elevation 1.2° > confirm the dat
 e. Use the AR view on site.\nHeights are approximate. Fine tune by a few m
 etres on the day.\n\nSOURCES\nMoon phases: US Naval Observatory 2027 table
  (aa.usno.navy.mil).\nMoon and sun positions: computed with Skyfield and J
 PL DE421\, with standard refraction.\nCoordinates: OpenStreetMap. Ground h
 eights: SRTM 30 m via OpenTopoData.\nTide predictions: Bureau of Meteorolo
 gy 2027 tide tables\, Copyright Commonwealth of Australia 2026. Based on B
