   92.0°\n18:59  altitude  2.7°\, azimuth  91.4°\n\nCAMERA POSITION\nCam
 era pin (the lookout itself): https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&qu
 ery=-33.57914\,151.30924\nWest Head Lookout\, West Head Road\, Ku-ring-gai
  Chase National Park NSW 2105\nSubject pin (Barrenjoey Lighthouse): https:
 //www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=-33.58019\,151.32983\nFrom the l
 ookout\, Barrenjoey Lighthouse is 1911 m away on bearing 93.5°.\nThe moon
  rises 0.5° left of the target\, roughly one moon width. Shift a few metr
 es along the rail to fine tune.\nStraight line from Neutral Bay: about 30 
 km.\n\nTIDES (BOM prediction\, Sydney (Fort Denison))\nNearest BOM standar
 d port. Broken Bay tides are similar in timing. The lookout is high above 
 the water\, so tide only changes the foreground.\nLow water Mon 15:21  0.2
 9 m\nHigh water Mon 21:31  1.75 m\nAt the alignment (18:46): about 1.15 m 
 and rising.\nPredictions exclude swell\, wind setup and wave run up. Check
  BOM coastal waters and swell forecasts on the day.\nSource table: https:/
 /www.bom.gov.au/ntc/IDO59001/IDO59001_2027_NSW_TP007.pdf\n\nFRAMING (Sony 
