 .52° wide\, about 17 m across at this distance.\nLandmark filling 60% of 
 the frame height: FE 70-200mm F2.8 GM OSS II with the 2x teleconverter at 
 400 mm\, or about 600 mm equivalent in APS-C crop mode.\nMoon dominant: FE
  70-200mm F2.8 GM OSS II with the 2x teleconverter at 400 mm (f/5.6) puts 
 the moon at 15% of frame height (23% in APS-C crop mode).\nTripod\, OSS of
 f on the tripod\, 2 s timer or remote\, shutter 1/125 s or faster at 400 m
 m.\nStart: ISO 200 to 400\, f/8\, expose for the moon. Bracket 3 frames at
  2 EV after sunset and blend.\n\nFIELD NOTES\n- NPWS: West Head gates clos
 e at 8.30pm during daylight saving and 6pm the rest of the year. Leave bef
 ore the gate closes.\n- Park entry is a vehicle day fee\, payable with the
  Park'nPay app.\n- The lookout is about 100 m above the sea\, so the moon 
